#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0258 expect=skipped domain=ADCM
#note "dataset ADCM; CMTRT (the TRT suffix detects OCCDS; no AEDECOD/AETERM, so AdamSubclassDetector's literal name test yields NO subclass). Scope.Subclasses.Include [ADVERSE EVENT] requires a positive detection -> skipped. Pins the OCCDS+AE gate pair. An AE block carrying the three join keys (and an AESEQ column on ADCM) is present so that the Subclasses scope is the ONLY reason to skip: without it the key's All_Or_None pairing group (PLAN-join-key-authoring-gate) would skip the rule as well, and this scenario would stop proving its own claim."
#library standard=adamig version=1-1
dataset ADCM
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col CMTRT   type=Char
col AESEQ   type=Num
---
S1 | 001 | ASPIRIN | 1
---

dataset AE label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char
col DOMAIN  type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col AESEQ   type=Num
---
S1 | AE | 001 | 1
